: "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2020-03-04T08:33:34Z", "updated_at": "2020-03-04T08:33:34Z", "body": "Thanks for the thoughts! Here are some of mine:\r\n\r\n> Could someone explain to me why we are blanket ignoring all QGC messages?\r\n\r\nI could guess that this was a legacy fix (e.g. MAVSDK was connecting to the first system it could find without checking if it had an autopilot), but that it may just work now. @julianoes an opinion here?\r\n\r\n> My suggestion is: as far as API goes, start with a void set_mavlink_id(uint8_t sid, uint8_t cid) or similar which allows for manual user setting of the SID and CID.\r\n\r\nWhat about having the `Configuration` object contain the SID and CID? I could imagine having an `AutopilotConfiguration` object that can take an SID and CID, and has a reasonable default, and a `CompanionConfiguation` that would only take the CID (because it auto-detects the SID). Could that do it? I think it is the same as your `set_mavlink_id` and `set_auto_mavlink_id` suggestions, but using OOP :innocent:.", "author_association": "COLLABORATOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/594390831/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null, "event": "commented", "actor": {"login": "JonasVautherin", "id": 2606672, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI2MDY2NzI=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2606672?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin", "html_url": "https://github.com/JonasVautherin", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/fo