1.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/pull/1001.patch", "merged_at": "2020-03-26T16:26:49Z"}, "body": "close #999.\r\n\r\nThis PR implements a a new `Configuration` class, replacing the old `enum class` of the same name. It allows for more flexibility and full control over the source system and component IDs of `Mavsdk` objects, in addition to fixing certain defaults to be more precise.\r\n\r\nThe `Configuration` class has 2 constructors - 1 which takes in the system and component id, for full manual control. The second one takes in a `UsageType` - which is an `enum class` inside `Configuration` which reimplements the same functionality as the original `enum class Configuration`. It allows the SDK to automatically choose an appropriate system and component ID based on the usage of the Mavsdk, whether it be `Autopilot, GroundStation` or `CompanionComputer`. I have attached an example (`examples/custom_configuration`) which can configure itself as any one of these or to a manual ID based on CLI arguments.\r\n\r\nOne thing mentioned by the issue still needs to be sorted out: In a couple of places, there is a blanket filter on any message with the system ID `255` - this is intended to filter out message from QGC, but is neither robust (as QGC's system ID can change) nor a good idea/even needed? @JonasVautherin thought that this was a remnant from when we used to connect to the first system we saw, but should no longer be needed as we now have more control over it. Still waiting for @julianoes or someone else's thoughts on this matter. This filtering happens in https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/blob/master/src/core/mavsdk_impl.cpp#L78 and https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/blob/master/src/core/udp_connection.cpp#L246.", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1001/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1001/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null}}, "event": "cross-referenced"}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/595005492", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/999#issuecomment-595005492", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/999", "id": 595005492, "node_id": "MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU5NTAwNTQ5Mg==", "user": {"login": "coderkalyan", "id": 35181624, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTgxNjI0", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35181624?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/coderkalyan", "html_url": "https://github.com/coderkalyan", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/coderkalyan/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/coderkalyan/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/coderkalyan/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/coderkalyan/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/coderkalyan/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/coderkalyan/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/coderkalyan/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/coderkalyan/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/coderkalyan/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2020-03-05T03:09:42Z", "updated_at": "2020-03-05T03:22:36Z", "body": "@JonasVautherin here's a PR that implements `Configuration`, still waiting for thoughts on what to do about QGC/ID 255 filtering. Having multiple subclasses proved very messy to implement for very limited benefit, so I just went with a single `Configuration` class with an `enum class UsageType` inside that, which provides similar functionality to the original `enum class Configuration`. Also not sure how to autodetect companion computer system ID.", "aut